 table([['Selected context','Practical diligence and state-law questions'],['Selected state: '+(answers.state||'Not provided'),'Use the selected state as the starting point—not necessarily the only state. Make a jurisdiction map for formation, offices, employees, research sites, manufacturing, distribution, clinician locations, patient/customer locations, and where data is collected. Identify the exact state statute, administrative regulation, licensing-board rule, and agency guidance for each activity. If multiple states are involved, repeat this review in each state.'],['Professional practice / telehealth / corporate practice','If the product or company provides, arranges, or influences clinical care, check state medical/nursing/pharmacy and other professional practice acts; telehealth licensure, consent, patient-location verification, standard-of-care, records, prescribing, and follow-up rules; corporate-practice-of-medicine restrictions; fee-splitting limits; and who may employ clinicians, set clinical protocols, control referrals, or share professional revenue. For a product-only vendor, confirm whether its actual functions cross into regulated clinical services.'],['Health data / consumer privacy / breach','Determine whether state comprehensive privacy law or a dedicated consumer-health-data statute reaches the company even if HIPAA does not. Review state health-record confidentiality, minors’ data, genetic/biometric data, consent and authorization, sale/sharing restrictions, geofencing/advertising restrictions where applicable, data subject rights, retention, processor contracts, security safeguards, and breach-notice deadlines. Map where the data subject resides and where the business operates.'],['Healthcare product / facility / distribution','For devices, diagnostics, software, or clinical services, check state facility, laboratory, professional, pharmacy, DME, home-health, or other licenses that depend on product claims and operational role. For a drug program, check state drug-manufacturer, wholesaler/3PL, pharmacy, distribution, controlled-substance, and research/compounding rules as applicable. Do not assume FDA clearance/approval replaces state licenses.'],['Entity, employment, and commercial operations','Confirm entity formation and foreign qualification; board/member authority; state tax and sales/use tax; employment, contractor, wage, invention-assignment, restrictive-covenant, and workplace rules; commercial contract and consumer-protection requirements; insurance; and local permits. Consider state securities notice filings and state-specific requirements if financing involves an offering.'],['Reimbursement / public programs / institutions','If billing or participating in Medicaid or state-regulated insurance, check state Medicaid coverage, telehealth reimbursement, provider enrollment, fee schedules, payer contract rules, and any applicable parity law. Review state university/health-system conflict, technology-transfer, procurement, research, and grant rules before promising rights or publication terms.'],['Organization: '+label(qs.find(q=>q.id==='company')||{options:[]},answers.company),'Confirm entity authority, board/member approvals, cap table, founder/employee IP assignments, conflicts, investor rights, and institution/health-system approvals.'],['Funding / grant / institution','Review award terms, permitted use, cost share, reporting, audit, publication, IP, government rights, domestic manufacturing, conflicts, and restrictions on exclusive licensing or subcontracting.'],['Securities / financing','If offering equity, debt, or investment interests, have securities counsel assess registration/exemption, disclosures, investor eligibility, solicitation, state notice filings, and transaction documentation. Do not rely on this report to select an exemption.']]);
